  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "In fringe cases, ever since an update in roughly October, users (such as myself) on lower end PCs have been unable to join some large worlds.\n\nWe end up being kicked to Home after spending too long in World Initialization. The issue is, before this update we were able to join and play in this world with 40-60 players without issue. It just took a bit to load in.\n\nSince that update, another bug cropped up, the Boot to Error World bug. To solve that bug, VRC increased the timeout timer. This also fixed the issue of not being able to join the world in question, for one of our players. But not myself or the other.\n\nCombined with the fact that we'd been able to join and play with no issues prior, we're fairly sure that the World Initialization Timeout is the actual cause and not our PCs running out of memory etc.\n\nMy request, on behalf of others in these fringe edge case situations where we KNOW we can run the map and VRChat is just telling us no anyway, we have the ability in the Debug settings to disable the timeout so we can just load in anyway.",
